      "lineNbr": 642,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-18T16:59:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the amount of log data we lost due to the overflow matches the length of the overflow message, then they could get back in sync. This is very unlikely though and would not really affect this fix. The fix is needed for all the cases where index and f_pos get out of sync. When index and f_pos are the same, both the old and new code work the same.",
      "parentUuid": "74e366a7_3573b989",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 642,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 642,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "293dc9c685c9694f727fc83133c17e857b349bc0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c4fdc8d8_85cc0122",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 642,
      "author": {
        "id": 1105075
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-18T17:12:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If the amount of log data we lost due to the overflow matches the length of the overflow message, then they could get back in sync. \n\nwhat if they doesn\u0027t match, is there a path that we make sure `log-\u003eput \u003d\u003d (u32)sfile-\u003eindex` after read.\n\nI am not just talking f_pos issue but in general how we can make sure log-\u003eput and sfile-\u003eindex kept in sync.",
      "parentUuid": "39fe1cb7_f90b1d9a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 642,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 642,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "293dc9c685c9694f727fc83133c17e857b349bc0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dfadcdd6_7df59fa2",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 642,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-05-18T17:16:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sfile-\u003eindex is the position where subsequent reads will start from, and the code in trusty_log_seq_* will read from there until \"put\". So once the reads are done, index and put will be in sync again.",
      "parentUuid": "c4fdc8d8_85cc0122",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 642,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 642,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "293dc9c685c9694f727fc83133c17e857b349bc0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
